===Etymology===
From {{etyl|ar|en}} {{m|ar|مَهْدِيّ||guided one}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/ˈmɑːdi/}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# {{lb|en|Sunni|_|Islam}} A leader who, according to Sunni [[eschatology]], will appear and restore peace and justice before the end of the world. {{defdate|from 17th c.}}
#: ''Ahmadis consider Mirza Ghulam Ahmed to be the '''Mahdi'''.''
#* '''2012''', {{w|Piers Brendon}}, ‘Beginning the Dissent’, ''Literary Review'', vol. 401:
#*: Al-Afghani was a polyglot Persian who became an international agitator, aspiring [...] to unify the Muslim masses behind the Caliph (or even the '''Mahdi''') and to become himself the Luther of an Islamic reformation.
# {{lb|en|Twelver Shiite|_|Islam}} {{w|Muhammad al-Mahdi|Muhammad b. Hasan al-Mahdi}}, the last of the Twelve [[imam|Imams]], born in 868 AD but believed alive and present in this world in a state of [[occultation]]; officially the [[head of state]] of the {{w|Islamic Republic of Iran}}; similarly to Sunni belief he will reappear before the end of time.

